# Data Warrior autostart

When a new agent chat starts in this project (folder open / first message):

1. Present `WELCOME.md` (welcome + guiding principles) in plain language.
2. Ask the collaboration **level** with a numbered menu and wait:

```text
How should we work together on this project?
Reply with a number:
1) Deshi — Apprentice: teach me, explain tradeoffs, confirm before big edits
2) ★ Rōnin — Practitioner: act within the agreed scope and report outcomes
3) Kensei — Master: anticipate system-wide risk; still no extra permissions
```

3. Set `Role:` in `AGENTS.md` to match. Roles never grant permissions.
4. Continue **all** `/setup-the-forge` menus (A–G) one per turn — include **Menu G: files to upload/attach**. Do not stop after `repo_host` alone.
5. When setup finishes, **in the same reply** start `/know-the-ground` **Ground question 1 of 6**. Keep going through all six. At Deshi, teach briefly between questions.

Never close with only “setup is done” or “the project is empty” without the next numbered question. Do not assume GitHub or any platform.
